## Flight report

**Left gate:** Crossed during the straight advance at decision k11 (the calibration-matching "one post at the frame edge, open room beyond" signature appeared at k11, and by k12 no posts remained in view, confirming transit). Getting lined up took much longer than planned — repeated single-post sightings (k3, k6, k8, k9) forced several R5 recovery turns and one R5 reverse (k9) before both posts and the gap were ever clearly seen together (briefly at k7). I can't certify the crossing went through the exact middle: I never held a clean "both posts symmetric, gap on tick" frame immediately before the final straight-through move, so the line-up was best-effort rather than verified-centered.

**Center gate:** Not crossed. After the left gate, the flight (mostly approved, following the trained trajectory) drifted to x≈2.2–2.6, y≈−0.9 to −1.0 with no gate posts ever appearing in the forward camera. I ran out of decisions (14 total) while still searching — the center gate was never located.

**Penguin:** Not confidently located. The downward camera showed a light blue/white object on the mats near the final position (x≈2.21, y≈−0.90) that could be the target or could be unrelated room furniture (no clear black-and-white pattern was visible) — I did not conclude either way per R3.

**Final pose:** x≈2.21, y≈−0.90, z≈1.45, heading≈−28°.

**Outcome:** Task not completed. Left gate crossing is likely (unverified centering); the center gate was never found and no hover over the penguin occurred. The single biggest cost was the left-gate line-up consuming 9 of 14 decisions on turn/reverse recovery before a clean crossing — too little budget remained to locate and cross the second gate.
